\"name\\\": \\\"REQ-3-2-1: Create a Repository with Owner, Visibility, and Initialization Options - Scenario 1\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The pre-provisioned `repo-owner` (`repo-owner@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`) owns the personal namespace and may create repositories there. The existing repository `acme-docs` is available for duplicate-name validation, while the candidate repository name is unused. the creation page from “New repository”; the personal namespace is selectable. If an organization namespace is selected, the user has permission to create repositories for that organization, and the candidate repository name is unused in the target namespace.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"GIVEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The user selects the target owner, enters a valid and unique repository name and optional description, selects “Private”, checks “Add a README file”, and clicks “Create repository”. Seed values: public repository `acme-docs`, private repository `secret-research`.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"WHEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The system enters the “owner/repository name” overview page, marked Private; the default branch contains a README file, and the commit history contains one initialization commit; the repository also appears in the target owner's repository list. Seed values: public repository `acme-docs`, private repository `secret-research`.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"After refreshing the overview page, the owner, visibility, README, and initialization commit remain; if the name is empty or duplicated, the user lacks organization-creation permission, or any step fails during creation, the system displays the reason and leaves no partially created repository. Seed values: public repository `acme-docs`, private repository `secret-research`.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}]}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"REQ-3-2-1: Create a Repository with Owner, Visibility, and Initialization Options - Scenario 2\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The pre-provisioned `repo-owner` (`repo-owner@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`) owns the personal namespace. The repository `acme-docs` already exists in that namespace.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"GIVEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor signs in as `repo-owner`, opens “New repository”, enters the existing repository name `acme-docs`, and clicks “Create repository”.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"WHEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The page displays the repository-name conflict message and does not display the existing repository overview heading.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}]}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"REQ-3-2-1: Create a Repository with Owner, Visibility, and Initialization Options - Scenario 3\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The pre-provisioned `repo-owner` (`repo-owner@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`) owns the personal namespace.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"GIVEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor signs in as `repo-owner`, opens “New repository”, leaves “Repository name” empty, and clicks “Create repository”.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"WHEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The page displays a repository-name-required validation message.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}]}], \\\"type\\\": \\\"ATOMIC\\\"}, \\\"effective_visual_references\\\": [], \\\"folder_context\\\": [\\\"{\\\\\\\"dependencies\\\\\\\": [], \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This product is a simplified GitHub collaboration platform. Unless an atomic requirement explicitly allows more than one role, every quoted user-interface name is the exact English accessible name of the control; the role, scope, and observable-state rules stated by each atomic 