-2-1: Create a Repository with Owner, Visibility, and Initialization Options - Scenario 2\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The pre-provisioned `repo-owner` (`repo-owner@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`) owns the personal namespace. The repository `acme-docs` already exists in that namespace.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"GIVEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor signs in as `repo-owner`, opens “New repository”, enters the existing repository name `acme-docs`, and clicks “Create repository”.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"WHEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The page displays the repository-name conflict message and does not display the existing repository overview heading.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}]}, {\\\"name\\\": \\\"REQ-3-2-1: Create a Repository with Owner, Visibility, and Initialization Options - Scenario 3\\\", \\\"steps\\\": [{\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor starts at the application home page in a fresh unauthenticated browser session. The pre-provisioned `repo-owner` (`repo-owner@example.test`, password `Valid-password-123!`) owns the personal namespace.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"GIVEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The visitor signs in as `repo-owner`, opens “New repository”, leaves “Repository name” empty, and clicks “Create repository”.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"WHEN\\\"}, {\\\"content\\\": \\\"The page displays a repository-name-required validation message.\\\", \\\"keyword\\\": \\\"THEN\\\"}]}], \\\"type\\\": \\\"ATOMIC\\\"}, \\\"effective_visual_references\\\": [], \\\"folder_context\\\": [\\\"{\\\\\\\"dependencies\\\\\\\": [], \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This product is a simplified GitHub collaboration platform. Unless an atomic requirement explicitly allows more than one role, every quoted user-interface name is the exact English accessible name of the control; the role, scope, and observable-state rules stated by each atomic 